<!--
    DisplayDeviceConfig for OnePlus Ace 3V (PJF110 / OP5CFBL1).

    Measured/stock data used here:
      Physical display id: 4630946583411818883 (port 131)
      Resolution: 1240x2772
      Logical density: 560
      Refresh modes: 60/90/120 Hz
      Ambient sensor: OPLUS Fusion Light Sensor (android.sensor.light)
      Brightness source: display_brightness_config_P_7.xml
      P_7 normal level 4095 ~= 508.468 nits
      P_7 extended level 4856 ~= 1115.050 nits
      HBM lux table mode: 30, first enter threshold: 10000 lux

    The P_7 brightness points are normalized against its extended maximum
    level 4856.  HyperOS on this donor reports a framework backlight minimum
    slightly below P_7 level 2 (3.66256e-4 vs 4.11862e-4).  Android's
    DisplayDeviceConfig requires the map to cover the complete framework
    backlight range, otherwise system_server aborts in
    constrainNitsAndBacklightArrays() and loops on bootanimation.  The 0/0
    compatibility anchor below lets Android clamp/interpolate to the real
    minimum while leaving every measured P_7 point unchanged.

    HBM transition 0.85 is aligned with the stock normal/HBM boundary near
    level 4095/4856.
-->
<displayConfiguration>
    <densityMapping>
        <density>
            <height>2772</height>
            <width>1240</width>
            <density>560</density>
        </density>
    </densityMapping>

    <screenBrightnessMap>
